  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ADD Latin America - Advocacy for alcohol policies to reduce harm</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Coalition for Americas&#xB4; Health, CLAS, a regional non-communicable diseases (NCDs) alliance for Latin America, aims to improve achievement of the SDGs, particularly Goal 3 on health, and strengthen the UHC agenda through building capacity of alcohol policy advocates and alliances in the LA region. CLAS will also contribute to a lower level of alcohol-related harm in selected countries in the region through advocacy for public health oriented National Alcohol Policies at country level. Alcohol harms women to an extent that is disproportionate with their own use, due to men&#x2019;s drinking in a context of harmful masculinities and gender norms, as well as weakly regulated alcohol sales. Conversely, effective alcohol policies will disproportionately benefit women, and this is a core gender equality objective for CLAS&#x2019; work in Latin-America.</narrative>
  </description>
